<title>UK: Pilkington H1 pretax profit down.</title>
<headline>Pilkington H1 pretax profit down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.0		    vs 7.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.75		   vs 1.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     75		     vs 104</p>
<p> Pretax (before except) 82		     vs 104</p>
<p>Turnover		   1.54 bln	     vs 1.37 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 75.0 to 79.0 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	93		     vs 108</p>
<p> Tax			 28		     vs 32</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 14</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 19</p>
<p>NOTE - Pilkington Plc said the exceptional item was the loss on the disposal of the Pilkington Barnes Hind contact lens business sold in October 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
